    rdfs:label "Evidence for Argol used in Woollen, Silk & Worsted Dyeing: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Products of the Vegetable Kingdom (1854; Project Gutenberg #15191), section BRAZIL WOOD"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "BRAZIL WOOD.--This very ponderous wood is obtained in Brazil from the Caesalpina Braziliensis, which yields a red or crimson dye, when united with alum or tartar, and is used by silk dyers."@en ;
